{
  "pyq_questions": [
    {
      "id": "q_jee_2024_ph_01",
      "examId": "jee_main",
      "exam": "JEE Main",
      "subjectId": "physics",
      "subject": "Physics",
      "chapterId": "rotational_motion",
      "chapter": "Rotational Motion",
      "topicId": "moment_of_inertia",
      "topic": "Moment of Inertia & Rolling Motion",
      "year": 2024,
      "shift": "29 Jan Shift 1",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "revisionZone": "high_yield",
      "ncertPages": "Class 11, pp. 164-172",
      "statementHtml": "<p>A solid sphere of mass $M$ and radius $R$ rolls without slipping down an inclined plane of inclination $\\theta$. The acceleration of the center of mass of the sphere is:</p>",
      "options": [
        { "key": "A", "html": "<p>$\\frac{5}{7} g \\sin \\theta$</p>" },
        { "key": "B", "html": "<p>$\\frac{2}{5} g \\sin \\theta$</p>" },
        { "key": "C", "html": "<p>$\\frac{1}{2} g \\sin \\theta$</p>" },
        { "key": "D", "html": "<p>$\\frac{7}{10} g \\sin \\theta$</p>" }
      ],
      "correctOption": "A",
      "numericalAnswer": null,
      "numericalTolerance": 0.0,
      "correctMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": -1,
      "solutionHtml": "<p>For a body rolling without slipping down an incline of angle $\\theta$, the linear acceleration is given by $a = \\frac{g \\sin \\theta}{1 + I / (M R^2)}$. For a solid sphere, $I = \\frac{2}{5} M R^2$, so $a = \\frac{g \\sin \\theta}{1 + 2/5} = \\frac{5}{7} g \\sin \\theta$.</p>",
      "commonMistakeType": "formula_mixup",
      "hasVideoSolution": true,
      "videoContentId": "vdo_ph_rot_01"
    },
    {
      "id": "q_jee_2024_ph_02",
      "examId": "jee_main",
      "exam": "JEE Main",
      "subjectId": "physics",
      "subject": "Physics",
      "chapterId": "rotational_motion",
      "chapter": "Rotational Motion",
      "topicId": "moment_of_inertia",
      "topic": "Moment of Inertia & Rolling Motion",
      "year": 2024,
      "shift": "30 Jan Shift 2",
      "type": "NAT",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "revisionZone": "trap_zone",
      "ncertPages": "Class 11, pp. 166-170",
      "statementHtml": "<p>A uniform disc of mass $4\\text{ kg}$ and radius $2\\text{ m}$ is rotating about an axis passing through its center and perpendicular to its plane with an angular velocity of $3\\text{ rad/s}$. Calculate its rotational kinetic energy in Joules.</p>",
      "options": [],
      "correctOption": null,
      "numericalAnswer": 36.0,
      "numericalTolerance": 0.1,
      "correctMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": 0,
      "solutionHtml": "<p>Moment of inertia of a uniform disc $I = \\frac{1}{2} M R^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 4 \\times 2^2 = 8\\text{ kg}\\cdot\\text{m}^2$. Rotational kinetic energy $K = \\frac{1}{2} I \\omega^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 8 \\times 3^2 = 36\\text{ J}$.</p>",
      "commonMistakeType": "calculation",
      "hasVideoSolution": true,
      "videoContentId": "vdo_ph_rot_02"
    },
    {
      "id": "q_jee_2023_ph_03",
      "examId": "jee_main",
      "exam": "JEE Main",
      "subjectId": "physics",
      "subject": "Physics",
      "chapterId": "electrostatics",
      "chapter": "Electrostatics",
      "topicId": "gauss_law",
      "topic": "Electric Flux & Gauss's Law",
      "year": 2023,
      "shift": "06 Apr Shift 1",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "revisionZone": "must_revise",
      "ncertPages": "Class 12, pp. 33-40",
      "statementHtml": "<p>A charge $q$ is placed at the center of the line joining two equal charges $Q$. The system of the three charges will be in equilibrium if $q$ is equal to:</p>",
      "options": [
        { "key": "A", "html": "<p>$-\\frac{Q}{2}$</p>" },
        { "key": "B", "html": "<p>$-\\frac{Q}{4}$</p>" },
        { "key": "C", "html": "<p>$+\\frac{Q}{4}$</p>" },
        { "key": "D", "html": "<p>$+\\frac{Q}{2}$</p>" }
      ],
      "correctOption": "B",
      "numericalAnswer": null,
      "numericalTolerance": 0.0,
      "correctMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": -1,
      "solutionHtml": "<p>For equilibrium of extreme charge $Q$, net force must be zero: $\\frac{k Q^2}{(2x)^2} + \\frac{k Q q}{x^2} = 0 \\implies \\frac{Q}{4} + q = 0 \\implies q = -\\frac{Q}{4}$.</p>",
      "commonMistakeType": "conceptual",
      "hasVideoSolution": true,
      "videoContentId": "vdo_ph_elec_01"
    },
    {
      "id": "q_jee_2024_ch_01",
      "examId": "jee_main",
      "exam": "JEE Main",
      "subjectId": "chemistry",
      "subject": "Chemistry",
      "chapterId": "chemical_kinetics",
      "chapter": "Chemical Kinetics",
      "topicId": "first_order_kinetics",
      "topic": "First Order Reactions & Half-Life",
      "year": 2024,
      "shift": "27 Jan Shift 1",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "revisionZone": "high_yield",
      "ncertPages": "Class 12, pp. 105-112",
      "statementHtml": "<p>For a first-order reaction, the time required for $99.9\\%$ completion is approximately how many times the half-life ($t_{1/2}$) of the reaction?</p>",
      "options": [
        { "key": "A", "html": "<p>$2$</p>" },
        { "key": "B", "html": "<p>$5$</p>" },
        { "key": "C", "html": "<p>$10$</p>" },
        { "key": "D", "html": "<p>$100$</p>" }
      ],
      "correctOption": "C",
      "numericalAnswer": null,
      "numericalTolerance": 0.0,
      "correctMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": -1,
      "solutionHtml": "<p>$t_{99.9\\%} = \\frac{2.303}{k} \\log\\left(\\frac{100}{0.1}\\right) = \\frac{2.303 \\times 3}{k}$. Since $t_{1/2} = \\frac{2.303 \\times 0.3010}{k}$, $\\frac{t_{99.9\\%}}{t_{1/2}} = \\frac{3}{0.3010} \\approx 10$.</p>",
      "commonMistakeType": "calculation",
      "hasVideoSolution": true,
      "videoContentId": "vdo_ch_kin_01"
    },
    {
      "id": "q_jee_2024_ma_01",
      "examId": "jee_main",
      "exam": "JEE Main",
      "subjectId": "mathematics",
      "subject": "Mathematics",
      "chapterId": "definite_integration",
      "chapter": "Definite Integration",
      "topicId": "kings_property",
      "topic": "Properties of Definite Integrals",
      "year": 2024,
      "shift": "31 Jan Shift 1",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "revisionZone": "high_yield",
      "ncertPages": "Class 12, pp. 341-349",
      "statementHtml": "<p>The value of the definite integral $I = \\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\frac{\\sqrt{\\sin x}}{\\sqrt{\\sin x} + \\sqrt{\\cos x}} \\, dx$ is:</p>",
      "options": [
        { "key": "A", "html": "<p>$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$</p>" },
        { "key": "B", "html": "<p>$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$</p>" },
        { "key": "C", "html": "<p>$\\pi$</p>" },
        { "key": "D", "html": "<p>$0$</p>" }
      ],
      "correctOption": "B",
      "numericalAnswer": null,
      "numericalTolerance": 0.0,
      "correctMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": -1,
      "solutionHtml": "<p>Using King's property $\\int_0^a f(x)dx = \\int_0^a f(a-x)dx$, adding both gives $2I = \\int_0^{\\pi/2} 1\\,dx = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\implies I = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$.</p>",
      "commonMistakeType": "formula_mixup",
      "hasVideoSolution": true,
      "videoContentId": "vdo_ma_int_01"
    },
    {
      "id": "q_neet_2024_bio_01",
      "examId": "neet",
      "exam": "NEET-UG",
      "subjectId": "biology",
      "subject": "Biology",
      "chapterId": "cell_unit_of_life",
      "chapter": "Cell: The Unit of Life",
      "topicId": "eukaryotic_organelles",
      "topic": "Mitochondria & Plastids",
      "year": 2024,
      "shift": "05 May Single Shift",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "revisionZone": "high_yield",
      "ncertPages": "Class 11 Biology, pp. 134-136",
      "statementHtml": "<p>Which of the following cell organelles contains its own double-stranded circular DNA and $70\\text{S}$ ribosomes?</p>",
      "options": [
        { "key": "A", "html": "<p>Golgi apparatus</p>" },
        { "key": "B", "html": "<p>Mitochondria</p>" },
        { "key": "C", "html": "<p>Lysosome</p>" },
        { "key": "D", "html": "<p>Endoplasmic Reticulum</p>" }
      ],
      "correctOption": "B",
      "numericalAnswer": null,
      "numericalTolerance": 0.0,
      "correctMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": -1,
      "solutionHtml": "<p>Mitochondria and chloroplasts are semi-autonomous organelles containing circular dsDNA and $70\\text{S}$ ribosomes (NCERT Class 11, p. 135).</p>",
      "commonMistakeType": "silly",
      "hasVideoSolution": true,
      "videoContentId": "vdo_bio_cell_01"
    },
    {
      "id": "q_neet_2023_bio_02",
      "examId": "neet",
      "exam": "NEET-UG",
      "subjectId": "biology",
      "subject": "Biology",
      "chapterId": "molecular_basis_inheritance",
      "chapter": "Molecular Basis of Inheritance",
      "topicId": "dna_replication",
      "topic": "DNA Packaging & Replication",
      "year": 2023,
      "shift": "07 May Single Shift",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "revisionZone": "trap_zone",
      "ncertPages": "Class 12 Biology, pp. 99-106",
      "statementHtml": "<p>In prokaryotes like <i>E. coli</i>, the DNA is held with some proteins that are positively charged in a region termed as:</p>",
      "options": [
        { "key": "A", "html": "<p>Nucleosome</p>" },
        { "key": "B", "html": "<p>Nucleoid</p>" },
        { "key": "C", "html": "<p>Chromatin</p>" },
        { "key": "D", "html": "<p>Solenoid</p>" }
      ],
      "correctOption": "B",
      "numericalAnswer": null,
      "numericalTolerance": 0.0,
      "correctMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": -1,
      "solutionHtml": "<p>In prokaryotes, negatively charged DNA is held with positively charged non-histone polyamine proteins in a region called the <b>Nucleoid</b> (NCERT Class 12, p. 99).</p>",
      "commonMistakeType": "conceptual",
      "hasVideoSolution": true,
      "videoContentId": "vdo_bio_mol_01"
    }
  ],
